      <li><a href="#agent-profile">Custom agent profile</a> · <a href="#instructions">Custom instructions</a> · <a href="#skills">Agent skills</a></li>
      <li><a href="#setup-steps">copilot-setup-steps.yml</a> · <a href="#mcp-config">MCP configuration</a> · <a href="#hooks">Hooks</a></li>
      <li><a href="#agentic-workflows">GitHub Agentic Workflows</a> · <a href="#copilot-cli">Copilot CLI</a> · <a href="#actions-blocks">GitHub Actions building blocks</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <!-- ================================================================= -->
  <h2 id="file-map">Where everything lives</h2>
  <Mermaid code={fileMap} caption="Customization lives in two places: versioned files in the repository, and settings that are not in Git." />
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="tbl t-slate">
      <thead><tr><th>File or setting</th><th>Location</th><th>Read by</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Repository instructions</td><td><code>.github/copilot-instructions.md</code></td><td>Chat, cloud agent, code review, CLI, IDEs</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Path-specific instructions</td><td><code>.github/instructions/**/*.instructions.md</code></td><td>Cloud agent, code review, CLI, IDEs</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Agent instructions</td><td><code>**/AGENTS.md</code> (nearest wins); root <code>CLAUDE.md</code> or <code>GEMINI.md</code></td><td>Cloud agent, CLI, IDEs; code review reads <code>AGENTS.md</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Prompt files</td><td><code>.github/prompts/*.prompt.md</code></td><td>IDEs only</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Custom agents</td><td><code>.github/agents/NAME.agent.md</code>; org/enterprise <code>agents/NAME.md</code> in <code>.github</code> or <code>.github-private</code></td><td>Cloud agent, Copilot app, CLI, IDEs</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Skills</td><td><code>.github/skills/</code>, <code>.claude/skills/</code> or <code>.agents/skills/</code>; personal <code>~/.copilot/skills/</code></td><td>Cloud agent, code review, CLI, Copilot app, VS Code</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Hooks</td><td><code>.github/hooks/*.json</code>; CLI also <code>~/.copilot/hooks/</code> and machine policy directories</td><td>Cloud agent, CLI (VS Code in preview)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Setup steps</td><td><code>.github/workflows/copilot-setup-steps.yml</code> (default branch)</td><td>Cloud agent; code review too, unless <code>copilot-code-review.yml</code> exists</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Repository MCP servers</td><td>Settings → Copilot → MCP servers (JSON)</td><td>Cloud agent and code review</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Firewall</td><td>Settings → Copilot → Internet access</td><td>Cloud agent and code review (configured separately)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Agent secrets</td><td>Settings → Secrets and variables → Agents</td><td>Cloud agent (<code>COPILOT_MCP_*</code> only to MCP servers)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Agentic workflows</td><td><code>.github/workflows/NAME.md</code> + compiled <code>NAME.lock.yml</code></td><td>GitHub Actions</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Enterprise managed settings</td><td><code>managed-settings.json</code>, usually in <code>.github-private</code>, or deployed by MDM</td><td>Copilot clients (CLI, IDEs)</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <!-- ================================================================= -->
  <h2 id="agent-profile">Custom agent profile</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={agentProfile} lang="markdown" label=".github/agents/test-specialist.agent.md" />
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="tbl t-violet">
      <thead><tr><th>Property</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>description</code></td><td>The only <strong>required</strong> property. Also what runtimes use to decide when to delegate — be specific.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>name</code></td><td>Optional display name; the filename (minus <code>.md</code> / <code>.agent.md</code>) is the identifier. Filenames may use only <code>. - _ a-z A-Z 0-9</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>tools</code></td><td>Omitted or <code>["*"]</code> = all; <code>[]</code> = none; aliases <code>read</code>, <code>edit</code>, <code>search</code>, <code>execute</code>, <code>agent</code>, <code>web</code>, <code>todo</code>; MCP tools as <code>server/tool</code> or <code>server/*</code>; unknown names ignored.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>target</code></td><td><code>vscode</code> or <code>github-copilot</code>; both when omitted.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>model</code></td><td>Model override; inherits the default when unset.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>disable-model-invocation</code></td><td><code>true</code> = must be selected manually; equivalent to the retired <code>infer: false</code> and takes precedence over it.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>user-invocable</code></td><td><code>false</code> = cannot be selected manually; programmatic use only. Default <code>true</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>mcp-servers</code></td><td>MCP servers for this agent only. Supports <code>{'${{ secrets.X }}'}</code> and <code>{'${{ vars.X }}'}</code>. Not used by IDE custom agents.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>metadata</code></td><td>Name/value annotations. Not used by IDE custom agents.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Body</td><td>The agent's prompt, up to <strong>30,000 characters</strong>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>handoffs</code>, <code>argument-hint</code></td><td>VS Code only — ignored by cloud agent on GitHub.com.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Profiles are versioned by the commit SHA of the file; a PR keeps using the version that started it. On a name
    clash, repository beats organization beats enterprise.
  </p>

  <!-- ================================================================= -->
  <h2 id="instructions">Custom instructions</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={repoInstructions} lang="markdown" />
  <CodeBlock code={pathSpecific} lang="markdown" label=".github/instructions/typescript.instructions.md" />
  <ul>
    <li><code>applyTo</code> takes comma-separated globs; <code>"**"</code> applies everywhere.</li>
    <li><code>excludeAgent: "code-review"</code> or <code>"cloud-agent"</code> keeps a file away from one agent.</li>
    <li>Personal instructions take priority over repository ones, which take priority over organization ones — but all relevant sets are sent.</li>
    <li>The first time Copilot opens a PR in a repository, it leaves a link to generate instructions automatically.</li>
  </ul>

  <!-- ================================================================= -->
  <h2 id="skills">Agent skills</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={skillMd} lang="markdown" label=".github/skills/github-actions-failure-debugging/SKILL.md" />
  <ul>
    <li>The file must be named <code>SKILL.md</code>, in its own lowercase, hyphenated folder; <code>name</code> and <code>description</code> are required, <code>license</code> optional.</li>
    <li>Scripts and resources in the folder are made available when the skill is used; reference them from the instructions.</li>
    <li><code>allowed-tools</code> pre-approves tools — pre-approve <code>shell</code> or <code>bash</code> only for skills you have reviewed and fully trust.</li>
    <li><code>gh skill</code> in GitHub CLI can search, install, update and publish skills.</li>
  </ul>

  <!-- ================================================================= -->
  <h2 id="setup-steps">copilot-setup-steps.yml</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={setupSteps} lang="yaml" label=".github/workflows/copilot-setup-steps.yml" />
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="tbl t-magenta">
      <thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Job name</td><td>Exactly <code>copilot-setup-steps</code>, or it is not picked up</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Customizable keys</td><td><code>steps</code>, <code>permissions</code>, <code>runs-on</code>, <code>services</code>, <code>snapshot</code>, <code>timeout-minutes</code> (max 59) — everything else ignored</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Branch</td><td>Must be on the default branch to take effect; it also runs as a normal workflow when changed, so you can test it</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Failure</td><td>A failing step skips the remaining setup; Copilot starts anyway</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Checkout</td><td><code>fetch-depth</code> is overridden; if you do not check out, Copilot does it after setup</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Runners</td><td>Ubuntu x64 or Windows 64-bit only; self-hosted must be ephemeral and needs the integrated firewall disabled</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <!-- ================================================================= -->
  <h2 id="mcp-config">MCP configuration</h2>
  <h3 id="mcp-repo">Repository settings (cloud agent and code review)</h3>
  <CodeBlock code={mcpJson} lang="jsonc" label="Settings → Copilot → MCP servers" />
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="tbl t-magenta">
      <thead><tr><th>Key</th><th>Applies to</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>type</code></td><td>All — required</td><td><code>local</code> / <code>stdio</code> (same thing), <code>http</code>, <code>sse</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>tools</code></td><td>All — required</td><td>Allowlist; prefer specific read-only tools, <code>["*"]</code> enables all</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>command</code>, <code>args</code></td><td>Local — required</td><td>How to start the server</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>env</code></td><td>Local</td><td>Literal values or <code>$COPILOT_MCP_*</code> references</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>url</code></td><td>Remote — required</td><td>Server endpoint; OAuth-only remote servers are not supported</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>headers</code></td><td>Remote</td><td>Literal values or <code>$COPILOT_MCP_*</code> references</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Reusing a VS Code <code>mcp.json</code>? Add a <code>tools</code> key to each server and replace <code>inputs</code>
    and <code>envFile</code> with <code>env</code>. Only <code>COPILOT_MCP_</code>-prefixed Agents secrets and variables
    are available to MCP configuration.
  </p>
  <h3 id="mcp-cli">Copilot CLI</h3>
  <CodeBlock code={cliMcp} lang="jsonc" />
  <p>
    <code>/mcp add</code> writes to <code>~/.copilot/mcp-config.json</code>; a repository <code>.mcp.json</code> adds
    workspace servers; <code>--additional-mcp-config</code> adds servers for one session;
    <code>--disable-builtin-mcps</code> turns off the built-in GitHub MCP server; <code>--add-github-mcp-toolset</code> and
    <code>--enable-all-github-mcp-tools</code> widen it beyond the CLI's default subset.
  </p>
  <p>
    For MCP allowlists in <code>managed-settings.json</code> and registry requirements, see
    <a href={`${href('skill-2-tools-environments')}#mcp-allowlists`}>Skill 2</a>.
  </p>

  <!-- ================================================================= -->
  <h2 id="hooks">Hooks</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={hooksFile} lang="json" label=".github/hooks/agent-hooks.json" />
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="tbl t-red">
      <thead><tr><th>Event</th><th>Fires</th><th>Can change the outcome?</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>sessionStart</code> / <code>sessionEnd</code></td><td>Session begins or resumes / ends</td><td>Start can inject context; end is notification</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>userPromptSubmitted</code></td><td>A prompt is submitted</td><td>Logging; prompt rewrite only for SDK hooks</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>preToolUse</code></td><td>Before every tool call</td><td><strong>Yes</strong> — allow, deny (with reason) or modify arguments</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>postToolUse</code></td><td>After a successful tool call</td><td>Can replace the result or add context</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>postToolUseFailure</code></td><td>After a failed tool call</td><td>Can add recovery guidance</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>agentStop</code> / <code>subagentStop</code></td><td>Main agent or a subagent finishes</td><td>Can block and force another turn (runaway guard after 8)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>subagentStart</code></td><td>A subagent is spawned</td><td>Can add context, cannot block</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>errorOccurred</code></td><td>An error occurs</td><td>No — logging and alerts</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>permissionRequest</code>, <code>preCompact</code>, <code>notification</code></td><td>CLI permission flow, compaction, notifications</td><td>Permission can allow or deny; others informational</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <CodeBlock code={denyOutput} lang="json" label="preToolUse output that blocks a call" />
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="tbl t-slate">
      <thead><tr><th>Behaviour</th><th>Rule</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Format</td><td><code>"version": 1</code>; each event is an array; entries are <code>command</code> (<code>bash</code>, <code>powershell</code>, <code>command</code>, <code>cwd</code>, <code>env</code>, <code>timeoutSec</code>) or <code>http</code> (<code>url</code>, <code>headers</code>)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Default timeout</td><td>30 seconds (<code>timeoutSec</code>); keep hooks under ~5 seconds — they run synchronously and block the agent</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Exit code 2</td><td>A warning for most events; a <strong>deny</strong> for <code>preToolUse</code> and <code>permissionRequest</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Other non-zero exits</td><td>Logged and skipped (fail-open) — except <code>preToolUse</code> command hooks, which fail <strong>closed</strong></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Timeouts</td><td>Always fail-open, even for <code>preToolUse</code> and policy hooks</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Several hooks</td><td>Run in order; for <code>preToolUse</code> any "deny" blocks the tool</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Cloud agent</td><td>Linux sandbox; only <code>bash</code> (or <code>command</code>) honoured; working directory <code>/workspace</code>; files discarded after the job (send logs via <code>http</code>); outbound calls need a firewall allow rule; <code>"ask"</code> = deny; <code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code> is not set</td></tr>
        <tr><td>CLI only</td><td>Machine-wide policy hooks (<code>/etc/github-copilot/policy.d/</code>, <code>C:\ProgramData\GitHub\Copilot\policy.d\</code>) load first and cannot be disabled by users</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <!-- ================================================================= -->
  <h2 id="agentic-workflows">GitHub Agentic Workflows</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={agenticWorkflow} lang="markdown" label=".github/workflows/daily-status.md" />
  <CodeBlock code={ghaw} lang="bash" label="GitHub CLI extension" />
  <ul>
    <li>The markdown body states intent; the frontmatter defines the boundaries. Both the <code>.md</code> and the compiled <code>.lock.yml</code> are committed to the default branch.</li>
    <li>Guardrails: read-only permissions by default, writes only through validated <code>safe-outputs</code>, secrets kept out of the agent's runtime, threat detection on proposed outputs, firewalled containers, role-based control of who can trigger or edit.</li>
    <li>Authentication: <code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code> with <code>copilot-requests: write</code> in organization repositories (the "Allow use of Copilot CLI billed to the organization" policy must be on), or a <code>COPILOT_GITHUB_TOKEN</code> fine-grained PAT for personal repositories.</li>
    <li>Cost: Actions minutes plus inference, tracked as AI credits (1 AIC = $0.01); <code>max-ai-credits</code> caps a run (default 1,000).</li>
  </ul>

  <!-- ================================================================= -->
  <h2 id="copilot-cli">Copilot CLI</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="tbl t-blue">
      <thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>-p</code>, <code>--prompt</code></td><td>Run one prompt non-interactively and exit; anything not pre-approved is denied</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>-s</code></td><td>Silent — clean output for scripts</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--no-ask-user</code></td><td>Disables the <code>ask_user</code> tool; the agent decides on its own</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--allow-tool</code> / <code>--deny-tool</code></td><td>Pre-approve / forbid tools (deny wins); patterns such as <code>shell(git:*)</code>, <code>write(path)</code>, <code>Server(tool)</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--available-tools</code> / <code>--excluded-tools</code></td><td>Restrict which tools the model can see</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--allow-all-tools</code>, <code>--allow-all</code> / <code>--yolo</code></td><td>Grant everything (tools, paths, URLs) — sandboxes only; can be disabled by policy</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--agent=NAME</code></td><td>Use a custom agent</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--model</code></td><td>Pin the model for consistent automation</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--plan</code>, <code>--autopilot</code></td><td>Start in plan mode; keep working until the task is complete</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--max-autopilot-continues=N</code></td><td>Cap autopilot's automatic continuations — always set it in automation</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--fleet</code></td><td>Run the prompt with parallel subagents</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--continue</code>, <code>-r</code> / <code>--resume</code></td><td>Resume the latest session here, or pick one by ID or name</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>-w</code>, <code>--worktree</code></td><td>Run the session in its own Git worktree</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--secret-env-vars</code></td><td>Redact variables from shell and MCP environments (<code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code> and <code>COPILOT_GITHUB_TOKEN</code> are redacted by default)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>--share=FILE</code>, <code>--share-gist</code></td><td>Export the session transcript as evidence</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="tbl t-blue">
      <thead><tr><th>Slash command</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>/plan</code> · <kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Tab</kbd></td><td>Plan mode; cycling further reaches autopilot</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/agent</code></td><td>Choose a custom agent</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/fleet</code></td><td>Parallel subagent execution of a plan</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/delegate</code> or an <code>&amp;</code> prefix</td><td>Hand the task to Copilot cloud agent (branch + draft PR)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/research</code>, <code>/review</code>, <code>/security-review</code></td><td>Built-in research, code-review and security-review agents</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/context</code>, <code>/compact</code></td><td>Show context usage; summarize history (auto at ~80%)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/rewind</code> · <kbd>Esc</kbd> <kbd>Esc</kbd></td><td>Roll back conversation, optionally restoring files</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/clear</code>, <code>/new</code></td><td>Start a fresh conversation</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/allow-all</code> (<code>/yolo</code>), <code>/reset-allowed-tools</code></td><td>Grant all permissions for the session; revoke granted permissions</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>/mcp</code></td><td>Add, list, enable, disable and authenticate MCP servers</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <Callout type="warn" title="Package and command names">
    <p>
      The CLI is installed with <code>npm install -g @github/copilot</code> and runs as <code>copilot</code>. Some Learn
      material shows <code>npx @github/copilot-cli</code> or a <code>copilot agent run</code> subcommand; neither matches
      the current documentation, so read such options for their intent (programmatic run, a named agent, restricted
      tools) rather than their exact spelling.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <!-- ================================================================= -->
  <h2 id="actions-blocks">GitHub Actions building blocks</h2>
  <CodeBlock code={actionsBlocks} lang="yaml" />
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="tbl t-slate">
      <thead><tr><th>Building block</th><th>Why it matters for agents</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>permissions</code></td><td>Least privilege; set a read-only default and elevate per job</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>concurrency</code></td><td>Stops overlapping runs; key on workflow and ref; a fixed group serializes deploys</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>environment</code></td><td>Required reviewers, wait timers and environment-scoped secrets gate risky jobs</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Step outputs (<code>$GITHUB_OUTPUT</code>) and job <code>outputs</code></td><td>Explicit contracts for passing plans and risk ratings between steps and jobs</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>needs</code></td><td>Sequencing and fan-in</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>workflow_run</code></td><td>Start one workflow when another completes</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>if: github.event_name == 'pull_request'</code></td><td>Defensive gating so PR-only logic never runs on other triggers</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Contexts</td><td><code>github.*</code> event metadata, <code>vars.*</code> central configuration, <code>env.*</code> runtime variables</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>actions/upload-artifact</code> / <code>download-artifact</code></td><td>Durable evidence and cross-job handoff; <code>retention-days</code> overrides the default 90</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>$GITHUB_STEP_SUMMARY</code></td><td>Human-readable evidence on the run page</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code> triggers</td><td>Events created with <code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code> mostly do not start new workflow runs, preventing loops; PATs and GitHub App tokens can — design against recursion</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

